Z||000000||Richard Parnell||12-16-1999||02:05 PM||||Hey guys.  Still working on my clutch.  I am waiting for new slave and master.  In the meantime I'm still fooling with the old set up.  It'll work for a while then get hard to shift again.  I did notice that when I have the resevoir cap off and pump the clutch that a small drizzle of fine air bubbles will come up out of the hole going into the cylinder.  What do you think.  Leaky master?  I got tired of that so I thought that I'd try another suggestion and put some thicker fluid in the system (Mobile 1 type) it works for a while but as I'm driving and go to put the clutch in there is absolutly nothing until I pump the clutch 4-5 times then will shift for a few seconds.  So thicker fluid only accentuated the problem.  It looks like I have no choice but to replace?||||reg||9
Z||000001||Richard Parnell||12-16-1999||03:07 PM||||Replaced mobile 1 with ATF.  The Mobile 1 was way too thick for the system.  Atf seems to hold a little pressure.  The whole thing is futile though until I get the new cylinders.  I'm rambling  no one around here thinks I'm sane any more and they certainly don't want to talk about Fieros. I just want to drive my car.Here I am posting replies to myself, pathetic.||||reg||11
