Z||000007||Richard Parnell||12-17-1999||12:05 AM||||Fianlly got my car to shift smoothly.  In fact it is smoother than ever.  Tried replacing the DOT3 with Mobile 1 .  Oil was too thick.  Rplaced with ATF.  That took a while because the oil was hard to push out with ATF until I lifted the front of the car utilizing the Famous Gravity Feed Method.  Shifted but still with a little grinding and binding.  (It didn't shift at all before).. Went out during lunch to check if the clutch pedal may be bent .  Noticed that the banjo was sliding a bit to one side on the bushing I had installed on the pedal some time ago.  Got some wahers and inserted them to keep the banjo straight into the master cylinder.  That 1/16 to 1/8 of an inch of throw made the difference.  I also think the angle was allowing air to enter the master.  Thanks to everyone out there in helping me use my brain and solve this problem.  I spent a good part of the day driving and reveling in the smoothness of the shifting.  Now I feel like I can move on to other projects with DA CAR. I owe everyone.||||reg||6
Z||000008||Patrick||12-17-1999||12:50 AM||||<BR>Glad to hear the news...||||reg||14
Z||000009||LOWRIDEGT||12-17-1999||01:12 AM||||You have to use a special tool to "power" purge all the air out. I've had 3 fieros w/ one displaying the same syptoms your having. I was able to properly bleed my first fiero but my last one I replaced slave and master with no luck in engaging the clutch until I took it to a dealership and got *&$#<BR>into having them do it. Good Luck- ||||reg||1
